# Product add on documents

Wherever the user adds a **product line** (PO, sales, stock, invoice, RMA, …), use the purchase-order format. Do not invent a plain search, “Add line” only, or a filter-less bar.

Canonical: `ProductSearchAdd` in `apps/web/src/components/products/product-search-add.tsx` (also `docs/ERP-UI-COMMON.md` §6).

```tsx
// ✅ [ ListFilter ][ 🔍 Name, SKU, barcode, or serial     + ]
// ❌ <input />  or  <button>Add product</button>  or  search without filter/plus
```

- Left: brand/category filter toggle with a caret (`h-9`, `border-r-0`; active `#00a09d`); the panel opens under the bar at full bar width, active filters show as removable chips inside the search box, and the panel never shows together with the results list
- Middle: typeahead SKU/name, **barcode scan**, or **serial number** (adds the matching product)
- Right: plus → quick-add product
- Square `h-8`, `rounded-none`. Extract/reuse; do not fork.

Not for catalog “New product” pages or merchandising/portal browse pickers.
